# A double-click on a space's name in the sidebar renames the space, as a double-click on a tab
# renames the tab (asked on X, 27 Nov 2026). A click on the header still collapses or expands the
# pinned tabs at once, as in Arc; the double-click's first click has done that by the time the
# second arrives, so the second puts the pinned tabs back and opens the name field. The clicks go
# through the event queue to the header, as the pointer's would.
budget rss=800 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=pinned
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://action/pinTab
wait 1
# The header row is 8,195, 312x36: its icon box (and the chevron) to x 39, the name from x 44.
cra://debug?snapshot=SpaceHeaderView&out=/dev/null
expect-log snapshot: SpaceHeaderView at 8,195 size 312x36

# One click on the name collapses the pinned tabs straight away.
cra://debug?clickAt=80,213
wait 1
cra://debug?browserWindows=click
expect-log Cra browser windows click: .* pinnedCollapsed=1

# A double-click on the name opens the field and leaves the pinned tabs collapsed, as they were.
cra://debug?clickAt=80,213&clicks=2
expect-log space header double-click: rename, pinned tabs put back
wait 0.5
cra://debug?browserWindows=field
expect-log Cra browser windows field: .* pinnedCollapsed=1
cra://debug?key=Q,12,0
cra://debug?key=x,7,0
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,0
wait 1
cra://debug?browserWindows=renamed
expect-log Cra browser windows renamed: kind=normal space=Qx .* pinnedCollapsed=1

# On the icon box a double-click is the chevron's: it collapses and expands, and renames nothing.
cra://debug?clickAt=26,213&clicks=2
wait 1
cra://debug?browserWindows=chevron
expect-log Cra browser windows chevron: kind=normal space=Qx .* pinnedCollapsed=1
cra://debug?checkStore=1
